From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t3code-customize <t3code-customize@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:45:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 12/14] Local: let theme CSS name images in the themes
 directory

Theme CSS may hold 20,000 characters, so an embedded background image has
to stay near 10 KB and looks blurred at window size. A theme can now name an
image file instead: url(theme-file:NAME) points at an avif, webp, png, jpg or
gif of up to 4 MB that sits next to the theme files.

The server reads the image through the same guarded read as theme files and
serves the theme with it inlined as a data: address, so clients still load
nothing by address and their check is unchanged. Served CSS gets its own,
larger length limit. Reading a theme back returns the file as written, and
the web client no longer stores CSS that large for its boot paint.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
